{"_id":"68a7362e8ec3d8323af1c4b1","nodeId":"P_Di-XPSDITmU3xKQew8G","roadmapSlug":"python","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:26.571Z","description":"# OOP\n\nIn Python, object-oriented Programming (OOPs) is a programming paradigm that uses objects and classes in programming. It aims to implement real-world entities like inheritance, polymorphism, encapsulation, etc., in programming. The main concept of OOPs is to bind the data and the functions that work on that together as a single unit so that no other part of the code can access this data.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"Object Oriented Programming in Python","url":"https://realpython.com/python3-object-oriented-programming/","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae38a"},{"type":"video","title":"Object Oriented Programming (OOP) In Python - Beginner Crash Course","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=-pEs-Bss8Wc/","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae38b"},{"type":"video","title":"OOP in Python One Shot","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ej_02ICOIgs","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae38c"},{"type":"video","title":"Python OOP Tutorial","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IbMDCwVm63M","_id":"6a75d319b0650226a50ae38d"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-07T12:44:09.455Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[{"_id":"6a5e33faacf8c05faf5e1fd0","title":"DataCamp - Python Programming Fundamentals","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/L0YnzL"},{"_id":"6a5e33fdacf8c05faf5e2124","title":"DataCamp - Python Developer","partner":"DataCamp","type":"course","url":"https://datacamp.pxf.io/vDW623"}],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/python/content/P_Di-XPSDITmU3xKQew8G.md"}